---@class posthog.feature_flags.CreateFeatureFlagsRollOutToEveryoneRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field id number A unique integer value identifying this feature flag.
---@field version number|distilled.Null The `version` from your most recent read of this flag. The change is refused with 409 if anyone else changed the flag after that version. A flag written before versioning reads as `null`; send that back unchanged and it is read as 0, so the value a read returns is always one this accepts.
---@field variant_key? string|distilled.Null The variant every user gets. Required for a multivariate flag and rejected for any other flag, because a release condition decides who the flag serves and not which variant they get.

---@class posthog.feature_flags.CreateFeatureFlagsSetReleaseConditionRolloutRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field id number A unique integer value identifying this feature flag.
---@field condition_index number Zero-based position of the release condition in `filters.groups`, counted from the read that produced `version`.
---@field rollout_percentage number Percentage of the users matching that condition who are served the flag, 0 through 100. On a multivariate flag this is how many matching users get a variant at all, not how the variants are split between them. Fractional percentages such as 0.5 are accepted, the same as a write that sends `filters`.
---@field version number|distilled.Null The `version` from your most recent read of this flag. The change is refused with 409 if anyone else changed the flag after that version. A flag written before versioning reads as `null`; send that back unchanged and it is read as 0, so the value a read returns is always one this accepts.

