---The body every DRF exception on these actions renders as.
---
---`ErrorResponseSerializer` declares a single `error` key, which no response on this viewset
---produces: the project exception handler renders this envelope instead. Declaring the wrong
---shape reaches the generated clients and the MCP tools, where an agent reads a key that is
---never there.
---@class posthog.feature_flags.FlagActionError
---@field type string Error class, for example `validation_error`.
---@field code string Machine-readable reason, for example `invalid_input`.
---@field detail string Human-readable description of what was refused.
---@field attr string|distilled.Null Request field the error belongs to, or null when it belongs to no single field.

---The 409 body an approval policy produces, which differs from every other error here.
---
---Raised through the approvals mixin rather than the exception handler, so it carries the
---change request it opened instead of the `type`/`attr` envelope.
---@class posthog.feature_flags.FlagApprovalConflict
---@field code string `approval_required` when this call opened the change request, `change_request_pending` when one was already open for the same action.
---@field status string Always `approval_required`.
---@field detail string Human-readable description of the policy that gated the change.
---@field message string Same text as `detail`.
---@field resource_type string Resource the change request targets, `feature_flag` here.
---@field resource_id string Id of the flag the change request targets.
---@field change_request_id string Id of the change request that was opened.
---@field change_request any The change request that was opened, serialized in full.
---@field required_approvers any Who can approve the change request.

---The 400 body a soft-deleted flag produces, which differs from every other error here.
---
---Built as a plain response rather than raised, so it carries neither the `type` nor the
---`attr` the exception handler's envelope has.
---@class posthog.feature_flags.FlagDeletedRejection
---@field success boolean Always `false`.
---@field error string Human-readable reason, naming the restore the caller has to do before retrying.

---The 400 body a change matching several approval policies produces.
---
---Raised through the approvals mixin rather than the exception handler, so it carries the
---policies that matched instead of the `type`/`attr` envelope.
---@class posthog.feature_flags.FlagPolicyConflict
---@field code string Always `policy_conflict`.
---@field error string Human-readable reason the change could not be gated.
---@field conflicting_policies any The approval policies that matched this change.
---@field guidance string How to split the change so each policy applies on its own.

