---@class posthog.feature_flags.ListFeatureFlagsRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field active? posthog.feature_flags.ListFeatureFlagsRequestActive|string 'true' and 'false' filter on serving state, the flag's `active` column. 'STALE' returns enabled flags only, so a disabled flag is never STALE. An enabled flag matches when its last recorded `$feature_flag_called` event is more than 30 days old. With no recorded event, it matches when it is at least 30 days old and either stores `filters` as `{}` or serves one result to everyone through a release condition at 100% with no property filters. A flag with no recorded event and an empty `groups` list does not match, even when its `status` reads STALE. The reverse also happens: a multivariate flag matches when a variant is at 100% under a release condition at 100% with no property filters, or when that condition names a variant. Its `status` can still read ACTIVE, because an earlier variant in the list or an earlier targeted condition can serve a different result. In a flag of either type that mixes person and group aggregation, the filter also counts a group-aggregated condition at 100% with no property filters, which `status` does not. An SDK that sends no `$feature_flag_called` event leaves no record, so a STALE flag can still be in use.
---@field archived? boolean Filter by archived state. When omitted, archived flags are excluded.
---@field created_by_id? string Filter by the user(s) who created the feature flag. Accepts a single user ID, or a JSON-encoded / comma-separated list of user IDs to match any of them.
---@field deleted? boolean Pass `true` to list only soft-deleted flags, which can be restored, archived or not. When omitted, deleted flags are excluded.
---@field eligible_for_experiment? posthog.feature_flags.ListFeatureFlagsRequestEligibleForExperiment|string When 'true', only return flags that can back an experiment: multivariate with 2-20 variants. Any other value is ignored.
---@field evaluation_runtime? posthog.feature_flags.ListFeatureFlagsRequestEvaluationRuntime|string Filter feature flags by their evaluation runtime.
---@field excluded_properties? string JSON-encoded list of feature flag keys to exclude from the results.
---@field excluded_tags? string JSON-encoded list of tag names to exclude. Flags carrying any of these tags are filtered out.
---@field has_evaluation_contexts? boolean Filter feature flags by presence of evaluation contexts. 'true' returns only flags with at least one evaluation context, 'false' returns only flags without.
---@field key? string Filter by exact feature flag key match. Case insensitive.
---@field limit? number Number of results to return per page.
---@field offset? number The initial index from which to return the results.
---@field search? string Search by feature flag key or name. Case insensitive. Spaces, underscores, and hyphens count as the same separator.
---@field tags? string JSON-encoded list of tag names to filter feature flags by.
---@field type? posthog.feature_flags.ListFeatureFlagsRequestType|string

---@alias posthog.feature_flags.ListFeatureFlagsRequestActive "STALE"|"false"|"true"

---@alias posthog.feature_flags.ListFeatureFlagsRequestEligibleForExperiment "true"

---@alias posthog.feature_flags.ListFeatureFlagsRequestEvaluationRuntime "all"|"client"|"server"

---@alias posthog.feature_flags.ListFeatureFlagsRequestType "boolean"|"experiment"|"multivariant"|"remote_config"

